  "summary": "Replaying GSS-TSIG signed UDP messages can result in memory corruption in \"`named`\".  An attacker who can capture a…",
  "details": "Replaying GSS-TSIG signed UDP messages can result in memory corruption in \"`named`\".  An attacker who can capture a previously signed UDP message can replay it while the negotiated TSIG key is still valid. By also sending crafted queries to a zone the attacker controls, the attacker may potentially achieve remote code execution.\nThis issue affects BIND 9 versions 9.11.0 through 9.18.50, 9.20.0 through 9.20.29, 9.21.0 through 9.21.26, 9.11.3-S1 through 9.18.50-S1, and 9.20.9-S1 through 9.20.29-S1.",
  "severity": [
